{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/972551-anyone-else-notice-a-lot-of-nietzche-in-mage","id":972551,"title":"Anyone else notice a lot of Nietzche in Mage?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-19T08:53:08-07:00","id":972551,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Anyone else notice a lot of Nietzche in Mage?","content":"I mean if you think about it, the climb to ascension seems much like Nietzche's Overman.<br /> <br /> You have the sleepers, who believe in the world as it is. Things are the way they are, and they have faith in that. Until something happens, and they wake up. They become a mage, and realize the world doesn't have rules. And so they embrace rules of their own making. They go from having values imposed upon them, to imposing the values they choose.<br /> <br /> This is why the increase in Arete is a step closer to ascension. With more power, the easier it is to impose YOUR values and break free of external values.<br /> <br /> And this is also why the Nephandi are so reviled by Mages, aside from the whole totally evil omnicidal maniac thing, Nephandi go through this process. And then they don't impose their values on the universe. They simply stop at the tearing down phase. They point out the meaninglessness of it all, and then do nothing to fix that.<br /> <br /> The Mage rejects reality and substitutes their own. The Nephandus just rejects reality.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T11:41:00-07:00","id":972609,"title":"","content":"There is a lot of modern and post-modern philosophy in Mage: the Navel-Gazing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T12:17:54-07:00","id":972634,"title":"","content":"And even older than that: there is also a lot of Kant,Hegel and Schopenhauer,Heraclitus,Plato and so on.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 09-19-2016, 03:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T12:24:23-07:00","id":972638,"title":"","content":"The Overman doesn't care a fig about the self-enslaved. So the Traditions are Nietzchean. The Ethos of the Union is directly opposed to this with the stated goal of universal Ascension. (I can't imagine anything more Non-Nietzchean than that). <br /> <br /> Guess who gets painted with the brush of &quot;Nietzchean Social Darwinists&quot; as bad guys and who gets to be the good guy expressing the value of personal freedom and self-worth?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T04:35:13-07:00","id":973038,"title":"","content":"The Niestzche's \u00dcbermesnch doesn't obey the Jew-Christian ethic, the &quot;master-slave morality his own moral code. For me that is a psycopath like Jeffrey Barantheon and Ramsay Bolton from &quot;Games of Thrones&quot;. <br /> <br /> To be a awakened doesn't mean be better, but only to have supernatural powers. Please, don't behave like a stupy rich kid If your PC doesn't respect the human dignity, then all his words about the Ascesion are a lie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T04:57:47-07:00","id":973042,"title":"","content":"The whole Ascension side of it certainly has shades of Nietzche.<br /> <br /> Though I think that mages awakening for the first time and gradually becoming more and more dissociated with sleeper reality is more like Plato's Analogy of the Cave.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T12:56:33-07:00","id":973316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/972551-anyone-else-notice-a-lot-of-nietzche-in-mage?p=972638#post972638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Overman doesn't care a fig about the self-enslaved. So the Traditions are Nietzchean. The Ethos of the Union is directly opposed to this with the stated goal of universal Ascension. (I can't imagine anything more Non-Nietzchean than that).<br /> <br /> Guess who gets painted with the brush of &quot;Nietzchean Social Darwinists&quot; as bad guys and who gets to be the good guy expressing the value of personal freedom and self-worth?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, here we go again.<br /> <br /> The Traditions do not, as a whole, have a stated purpose when it comes to elevating, or even interacting with, Sleepers as a whole. The former Technocratic Traditions, at least in part, are interested in helping humanity as whole, at least tangentially, if not directly. The Cult of Ecstasy is filled with people wanting to expand the horizons of everyone, including Sleepers, and the Dreamspeakers seek balance between the worlds, which helps <i>everyone</i> in their minds. They're not all &quot;above the masses&quot; that you're painting them to be.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, the stated purpose of the Order of Reason and the Technocracy is the elevation and protection of mankind as a whole. Unfortunately, the execution of said purpose is often oppressive and narrow-minded, sometimes even dangerously zealous. Of course, you can even say that they've fallen from their purpose of working for the sake of humanity and only working to maintain their own power anymore. There are elements within the Union that see how the organization has gone off the rails, but they're effectively rebels within the machine.<br /> <br /> Relate that to Nietzche as you will.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6384-frozenfishy","name":"Frozenfishy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}